---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="The longer version of who I am.">
  <article class="about">
    <header>
      <div class="meta-label">About · Marco Ledesma</div>
      <h1>I started writing code in <span class="accent">2012</span>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Most of what I know I learned by being thrown into things I wasn't qualified for and figuring it out. The rest came from people generous enough to teach me. This site is partly an attempt to pay that forward.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where I've worked</h2>
      <p>
        I spent four and a half years at <strong>Spud Software</strong> in Michigan as a remote developer, working across whatever stack the next client needed. It was the kind of job where you ship a React Native app one quarter and a Rails admin panel the next, and you learn to read codebases quickly because you have to.
      </p>
      <p>
        After that I joined <strong>Leasecake</strong> as the first engineer. Spent four years as Principal Software Engineer, two as Director of Engineering. I built the original product end-to-end alongside the founder, then grew and managed the team as the company scaled. Lease accounting under ASC 842 is one of the more brutally specific domains I've worked in — the kind where a floating-point rounding artifact can become a customer-facing bug.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since August 2024 I've been at <strong>SendJim</strong>, first as Principal and now as VP of Engineering. We build campaign automation — direct mail, follow-ups, the connective tissue between a CRM and a mailbox — for small businesses, mostly home-services franchises.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm actually good at</h2>
      <p>
        Three things, mostly. <em>One:</em> taking a vague business problem and turning it into a system you can actually build and maintain. <em>Two:</em> reading a codebase nobody loves and figuring out what's worth saving. <em>Three:</em> writing the version of a doc, a ticket, or an explanation that the reader didn't know they needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm not the person you hire to invent a new database. I'm the person you hire when the database you have is fine but everything around it is on fire.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm interested in right now</h2>
      <p>
        Practical applications of LLMs as <em>tools</em> for engineers, not replacements for them. I built <a href="/projects">Sunny Bots</a> because I wanted the leverage of Claude Code without losing the structure of my own workflow. I think there's a lot of room for tooling in this space that respects the user's intelligence.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also increasingly interested in <em>teaching</em> — through writing, through internal documentation, through the long-form explainers that take a week to write and save the reader an afternoon. If you're working on something in that space I'd love to talk.
      </p>

      <h2>The non-work stuff</h2>
      <p>
        I live in Orlando with my family and two cats. I drive a Toyota Crown, which is a decision I have strong feelings about. I'm Peruvian (hence the GitHub handle). I occasionally try to install Linux on things that don't want Linux installed on them.
      </p>

      <h2>How to reach me</h2>
      <p>
        Email is best: <a href="mailto:hello@marcoledesma.com">hello@marcoledesma.com</a>. I read everything, I reply to most of it, and I'm especially happy to hear from people working on developer tools, technical writing, or anything involving small teams shipping serious software.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding: 80px 0 100px; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  header { margin-bottom: 80px; }
  .meta-label { margin-bottom: 24px; }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 6.5vw, 80px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  h1 .accent { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 800; }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
</style>
